WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.152 --> 00:00:04.568
- Turn fear on itself.

00:00:04.568 --> 00:00:05.788
- Feel fear quite strongly.

00:00:05.788 --> 00:00:07.247
- Fear is the fuel.

00:00:07.247 --> 00:00:08.503
- ...Undoes the fear.

00:00:08.503 --> 00:00:10.491
- I grandiose my way out of fear.

00:00:10.491 --> 00:00:11.324
- Fear.

00:00:11.324 --> 00:00:12.282
- Embrace that fear.

00:00:12.282 --> 00:00:13.622
- Transcend that fear.

00:00:13.622 --> 00:00:16.093
- Hello believe nation,
my name Evan Carmichael,

00:00:16.093 --> 00:00:18.370
my one word is believe, and I believe

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:19.706
that entrepreneurs will solve

00:00:19.706 --> 00:00:22.308
all of the worlds major challenges.

00:00:22.308 --> 00:00:23.853
And so to help you on your mission,

00:00:23.853 --> 00:00:28.250
today we're going to learn how
you can overcome your fears.

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:30.165
And as always guys, as
you're watching the video,

00:00:30.165 --> 00:00:31.668
if something really speaks to you,

00:00:31.668 --> 00:00:33.336
please leave it down in the comments below

00:00:33.336 --> 00:00:35.975
and put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired.

00:00:35.975 --> 00:00:38.046
And when you write it
down, it's much more likely

00:00:38.046 --> 00:00:41.129
to stick for yourself as well, enjoy.

00:00:42.882 --> 00:00:46.549
(grandiose orchestra music)

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:54.501
- The only way to deal with fear

00:00:54.501 --> 00:00:56.818
that I've found in my
life is a couple ways.

00:00:56.818 --> 00:01:00.054
One of those ways is to turn it on itself

00:01:00.054 --> 00:01:02.448
and ask yourself what am I afraid of?

00:01:02.448 --> 00:01:03.629
I'm afraid of that?

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:05.341
I've got to be more afraid of what

00:01:05.341 --> 00:01:07.333
I'm going to miss out on,
missing out on my mission,

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:08.396
missing out on who I'm supposed to be.

00:01:08.396 --> 00:01:10.759
In other words, if you're
not going to get rid of fear

00:01:10.759 --> 00:01:14.855
then use fear, use fear or it
uses you, it's that simple.

00:01:14.855 --> 00:01:16.642
So you got to say okay, what's the price

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:18.965
if I just stay doing
this, what's the price?

00:01:18.965 --> 00:01:20.955
I mean, I can really get scared

00:01:20.955 --> 00:01:23.112
if I learn all this and
I don't follow through.

00:01:23.112 --> 00:01:25.223
That's something to be scared about.

00:01:25.223 --> 00:01:27.300
And then that fear will
get you over your fear,

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:30.098
it'll push you through,
turn fear on itself.

00:01:30.098 --> 00:01:32.244
Second way you can do it is use what

00:01:32.244 --> 00:01:33.787
you've probably heard me
say, 'cause I've used it

00:01:33.787 --> 00:01:37.199
since I was 17, is my little
rocking chair test, right?

00:01:37.199 --> 00:01:39.110
I'm going to sit myself
in my rocking chair,

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:41.345
I'm 85 years old, I'm
looking back on my life,

00:01:41.345 --> 00:01:44.262
and say I didn't do this, or I did.

00:01:45.249 --> 00:01:47.935
- You're unusually
fearless and willing to go

00:01:47.935 --> 00:01:50.329
in the face of other people
telling you it's crazy.

00:01:50.329 --> 00:01:51.875
And I know a lot of pretty crazy people,

00:01:51.875 --> 00:01:53.423
you still stand out.

00:01:53.423 --> 00:01:54.563
Where does that come
from or how do you think

00:01:54.563 --> 00:01:56.469
about making a decision when everyone

00:01:56.469 --> 00:01:58.418
tells you this is a crazy idea?

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:00.779
Where do you get the
internal strength to do that?

00:02:00.779 --> 00:02:02.490
- Well first of all,
I'd say I actually think

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:06.573
I feel fear quite strongly,
so it's not as though

00:02:08.624 --> 00:02:10.252
I just have the absence of fear,

00:02:10.252 --> 00:02:12.687
I feel it quite strongly.

00:02:12.687 --> 00:02:15.368
But there are just times when something

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:17.847
is important enough, you
believe in it enough,

00:02:17.847 --> 00:02:20.738
that you do it in spite of the fear.

00:02:20.738 --> 00:02:22.168
- So speaking of important things...

00:02:22.168 --> 00:02:26.335
- People shouldn't think,
well I feel fear about this

00:02:27.651 --> 00:02:30.131
and therefore I shouldn't do it.

00:02:30.131 --> 00:02:33.871
It's normal to feel fear,
like there'd have to be

00:02:33.871 --> 00:02:37.682
something mentally wrong
if you didn't feel fear.

00:02:37.682 --> 00:02:39.180
- So you just feel it
and let the importance

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.330
of it drive you to do it anyway?

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:43.403
- Yeah, actually something
that can be helpful

00:02:43.403 --> 00:02:46.127
is fatalism, to some degree.

00:02:46.127 --> 00:02:48.449
If you just accept the probabilities

00:02:48.449 --> 00:02:50.616
then that diminishes fear.

00:02:54.184 --> 00:02:56.379
When starting SpaceX I
thought the odds of success

00:02:56.379 --> 00:03:00.767
were less than 10%, and I just accepted

00:03:00.767 --> 00:03:04.934
that actually, probably, I
would just lose everything,

00:03:05.945 --> 00:03:08.099
but that maybe we'd make some progress

00:03:08.099 --> 00:03:09.928
if we could just move the ball forward,

00:03:09.928 --> 00:03:12.561
even if we died, maybe
some other company could

00:03:12.561 --> 00:03:16.343
pick up the baton and
keep moving it forward,

00:03:16.343 --> 00:03:19.658
so that we'll still do some good.

00:03:19.658 --> 00:03:21.041
Yeah, same with Tesla.

00:03:21.041 --> 00:03:22.344
I thought the odds of a car company

00:03:22.344 --> 00:03:24.586
succeeding were extremely low.

00:03:24.586 --> 00:03:26.614
- There's always fear and
I even put it in Rocky 3

00:03:26.614 --> 00:03:28.520
that, you know, he's
'I'm afraid, I'm afraid'.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:33.286
But the fear is the fuel that
we use for overachievement.

00:03:33.286 --> 00:03:36.820
If I wasn't afraid at times
I wouldn't work as hard

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:39.016
because the fear is, I
don't want to slip back

00:03:39.016 --> 00:03:41.451
into mediocrity, I don't want to just say,

00:03:41.451 --> 00:03:43.236
okay I want to rest on my laurels.

00:03:43.236 --> 00:03:45.800
So I hear footsteps all the time,

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:48.164
and I know that I only have
a certain amount of time

00:03:48.164 --> 00:03:51.861
and I don't want to waste it
because it's gone so quickly.

00:03:51.861 --> 00:03:55.064
Since Rocky it's been almost
seven and a half, eight years,

00:03:55.064 --> 00:03:57.697
and I think Talia and I
are just overachievers

00:03:57.697 --> 00:04:01.463
because we know that
there's only a certain

00:04:01.463 --> 00:04:03.454
amount of productivity in a day

00:04:03.454 --> 00:04:04.955
and we don't want to waste it.

00:04:04.955 --> 00:04:06.671
- I'm a writer, I'm supposed
to be behind the scenes

00:04:06.671 --> 00:04:08.464
and everybody else is supposed
to be in front of the stuff.

00:04:08.464 --> 00:04:11.029
- Now she's finally in
front of the camera.

00:04:11.029 --> 00:04:12.577
The famously private woman talking

00:04:12.577 --> 00:04:15.053
about her epic struggles with anxiety

00:04:15.053 --> 00:04:17.049
and her fear of public speaking.

00:04:17.049 --> 00:04:19.165
What physiologically
happens when you're having

00:04:19.165 --> 00:04:21.319
that stage four panic attack?

00:04:21.319 --> 00:04:23.566
- There's a little bit
of panicked breathing,

00:04:23.566 --> 00:04:24.938
there's a lot of pacing back

00:04:24.938 --> 00:04:26.479
and forth and mumbling to myself.

00:04:26.479 --> 00:04:28.478
- [Reporter] Despite being
invited to every glamorous

00:04:28.478 --> 00:04:30.799
party in Hollywood, she'd make excuses

00:04:30.799 --> 00:04:32.876
saying she was just too busy,

00:04:32.876 --> 00:04:35.111
until one day her sister provoked her.

00:04:35.111 --> 00:04:37.966
- I was sort of going on
and on about all of the

00:04:37.966 --> 00:04:39.991
invitations that I'd received.

00:04:39.991 --> 00:04:42.061
And my sister finally cut in and said

00:04:42.061 --> 00:04:44.952
are you going to say yes
to any of these things?

00:04:44.952 --> 00:04:46.903
And I remember being very taken aback

00:04:46.903 --> 00:04:50.314
and saying no I'm busy I can't,

00:04:50.314 --> 00:04:53.154
And her sort of looking
at me like, that's insane,

00:04:53.154 --> 00:04:54.541
and at some point just saying,

00:04:54.541 --> 00:04:56.936
you never say yes to anything.

00:04:56.936 --> 00:04:59.144
And those words really sticking with me,

00:04:59.144 --> 00:05:00.512
because she was right.

00:05:00.512 --> 00:05:02.787
- And so this became a campaign to say

00:05:02.787 --> 00:05:04.818
yes to the things that scared you.

00:05:04.818 --> 00:05:06.900
- Yeah, to say yes to the
things that freaked me out.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.617
- And when you started saying
yes, what started to happen?

00:05:09.617 --> 00:05:13.283
- It's the doing of the thing
that sort of undoes the fear.

00:05:13.283 --> 00:05:15.721
- When you experience
moments of self-doubt,

00:05:15.721 --> 00:05:17.579
how do you approach getting
out of that dark place?

00:05:17.579 --> 00:05:18.650
- [Woman] Good question.

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:21.064
- I grandiose my way out of fear.

00:05:21.064 --> 00:05:23.462
(laughing)

00:05:23.462 --> 00:05:25.177
- [Robert] If you could imagine that.

00:05:25.177 --> 00:05:28.510
(laughing and applause)

00:05:30.259 --> 00:05:32.321
- [Woman] It's a good way, it's charming.

00:05:32.321 --> 00:05:34.599
- Literally it's like, okay,
I'm going to do one of the

00:05:34.599 --> 00:05:38.094
greatest car chases of all time.

00:05:38.094 --> 00:05:42.505
And if I don't I'm not as
talented as I thought I was.

00:05:42.505 --> 00:05:43.338
(audience laughs)

00:05:43.338 --> 00:05:45.851
And I will realize that there
is a ceiling to my talent,

00:05:45.851 --> 00:05:48.738
right now I don't think there
is, but if I don't do...

00:05:48.738 --> 00:05:49.799
(audience laughs)

00:05:49.799 --> 00:05:52.238
But if it's not one of the
greatest car chases of all time,

00:05:52.238 --> 00:05:54.477
then I failed and there
is a ceiling to my talent,

00:05:54.477 --> 00:05:56.423
I'm not as good as I thought I was.

00:05:56.423 --> 00:05:58.950
And I said that to
everybody, and was I scared?

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:03.575
(blank) yeah, I had
trepidation going all the way,

00:06:03.575 --> 00:06:07.526
'cause it's mine to fail, and it's failing

00:06:07.526 --> 00:06:09.468
in front of the mirror
too, 'cause I'll know

00:06:09.468 --> 00:06:10.807
if I did it or not and I'll be like,

00:06:10.807 --> 00:06:13.534
okay, you were not as good
as you thought you were.

00:06:13.534 --> 00:06:16.379
And that got me to Mount Everest.

00:06:16.379 --> 00:06:17.811
- It's true, I remember
at one point he goes,

00:06:17.811 --> 00:06:20.121
Robert, can you imagine you
and me doing this car chase

00:06:20.121 --> 00:06:21.877
together, how great it's going to be?

00:06:21.877 --> 00:06:23.426
And I'm like hey man,
you're on your own brother.

00:06:23.426 --> 00:06:25.948
(laughing)

00:06:25.948 --> 00:06:28.056
I ain't going out there man,
I got five (blank) kids.

00:06:28.056 --> 00:06:31.835
I'm not going to do no hundred
mile an hour bull(blank).

00:06:31.835 --> 00:06:34.468
You want to live the Vanishing
Point dream buddy? Live it.

00:06:34.468 --> 00:06:36.718
(laughing)

00:06:37.555 --> 00:06:38.491
And he did it all by himself

00:06:38.491 --> 00:06:39.831
and I'm so (blank) proud of him.

00:06:39.831 --> 00:06:41.734
- [Interviewer] Is that
the big difference between,

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:44.896
'cause I see you in your
basement like a Batman

00:06:44.896 --> 00:06:46.567
with all machines and stuff.

00:06:46.567 --> 00:06:48.758
It's really precise, I guess, and really

00:06:48.758 --> 00:06:52.172
you know what you put
and then you go live.

00:06:52.172 --> 00:06:54.449
What's the difference, the risk?

00:06:54.449 --> 00:06:57.449
- The risk, you know and the risk...

00:06:58.911 --> 00:07:02.933
I have stage fright and I
never confronted the risk,

00:07:02.933 --> 00:07:07.036
or when I did confront, you
know Belgium, year 2000.

00:07:07.036 --> 00:07:09.391
That was, you have no idea what

00:07:09.391 --> 00:07:12.193
it took then to get me to do it.

00:07:12.193 --> 00:07:14.068
- [Interviewer] And why did you say yes?

00:07:14.068 --> 00:07:16.951
- I had 1000 excuses why not do it,

00:07:16.951 --> 00:07:20.284
and then finally I did it, and it was...

00:07:24.915 --> 00:07:28.505
Exquisitely horrifying, that's
the only way I can put it.

00:07:28.505 --> 00:07:29.481
- [Interviewer] Complex.

00:07:29.481 --> 00:07:32.564
- Yes, it was very very very complex.

00:07:33.829 --> 00:07:37.449
And what was really good,
was right at the beginning,

00:07:37.449 --> 00:07:41.062
within like two seconds,
I played just the worst

00:07:41.062 --> 00:07:44.729
wrong note, and I could
either stop and cry,

00:07:46.145 --> 00:07:48.712
or I could laugh, alright?

00:07:48.712 --> 00:07:50.252
And it didn't kill me,
and nobody else out there,

00:07:50.252 --> 00:07:53.832
nobody was throwing anything,
you know? It was fine.

00:07:53.832 --> 00:07:58.256
Thank you to the people of
Ghent for not killing me

00:07:58.256 --> 00:08:00.397
and giving me the courage.

00:08:00.397 --> 00:08:04.564
And the absurdity, you have to
be able to laugh at yourself.

00:08:06.617 --> 00:08:09.013
And you have to learn
how to laugh at yourself.

00:08:09.013 --> 00:08:12.836
- If you say I'm a fraud,
they'll figure me out,

00:08:12.836 --> 00:08:14.345
I'll never be able to do it again,

00:08:14.345 --> 00:08:16.614
that's an artist's thought
process, you're an artist.

00:08:16.614 --> 00:08:18.278
If you're thinking like that, then you're

00:08:18.278 --> 00:08:19.486
on the right track,
because they all fell that.

00:08:19.486 --> 00:08:21.837
So there's always some
success that can come out

00:08:21.837 --> 00:08:23.458
even out of your
failures, in fact probably

00:08:23.458 --> 00:08:24.871
your biggest successes will come

00:08:24.871 --> 00:08:26.455
directly from your failures.

00:08:26.455 --> 00:08:28.328
So you should almost, take that Winston

00:08:28.328 --> 00:08:29.743
Churchill quote, it's my favorite.

00:08:29.743 --> 00:08:31.812
"Success is moving from one failure

00:08:31.812 --> 00:08:33.962
to the next with great enthusiasm."

00:08:33.962 --> 00:08:36.077
You should be very enthusiastic
about your failures

00:08:36.077 --> 00:08:37.859
because you're going to learn something.

00:08:37.859 --> 00:08:39.776
You're going to go that
way when everyone else

00:08:39.776 --> 00:08:41.966
is going that way, and
you're going to stumble,

00:08:41.966 --> 00:08:44.414
but you're also going to
stumble upon something

00:08:44.414 --> 00:08:45.247
that no one ever thought of.

00:08:45.247 --> 00:08:46.590
So you know, you just
keep going and keep going

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:48.131
and you're going to fail and then rise up

00:08:48.131 --> 00:08:49.876
and then fail again,
and that's the journey.

00:08:49.876 --> 00:08:51.221
Up and down, man.

00:08:51.221 --> 00:08:54.555
- Most of us that come from
just normal backgrounds,

00:08:54.555 --> 00:08:57.768
we don't see ourselves
doing abnormal things.

00:08:57.768 --> 00:08:59.837
The world is full of people
who were born on third

00:08:59.837 --> 00:09:01.705
and think they hit a
triple and they've got

00:09:01.705 --> 00:09:04.419
all this confidence, all this stuff.

00:09:04.419 --> 00:09:06.855
For most of us, it's not that way.

00:09:06.855 --> 00:09:09.007
We don't think we're wired

00:09:09.007 --> 00:09:11.646
or programmed to do something great.

00:09:11.646 --> 00:09:15.813
Well I'm telling ya, that
thought is nothing but a fear.

00:09:16.803 --> 00:09:20.994
Nothing but a doubt, it's
what holds you in place.

00:09:20.994 --> 00:09:25.161
You got to work hard on
understanding you have within you

00:09:26.478 --> 00:09:30.424
the power to change, the
power to do something great.

00:09:30.424 --> 00:09:33.928
And those fears are going
to crop up particularly

00:09:33.928 --> 00:09:36.124
in the middle of the
night when you wake up

00:09:36.124 --> 00:09:38.849
and you're scared to
death about what to do.

00:09:38.849 --> 00:09:42.347
They're going to crop up and
they're going to hold you in place.

00:09:42.347 --> 00:09:44.499
Quite often if you're
trying something different

00:09:44.499 --> 00:09:46.853
they crop up in the middle of your dreams,

00:09:46.853 --> 00:09:48.729
when you're asleep at night those

00:09:48.729 --> 00:09:50.896
fears and doubts creep in.

00:09:52.214 --> 00:09:55.881
Understand they're not
real, they are things

00:09:57.257 --> 00:10:00.388
in your head that have been programmed

00:10:00.388 --> 00:10:02.708
into you by your past life.

00:10:02.708 --> 00:10:06.214
Wrestle with those fears,
you'll never conquer them

00:10:06.214 --> 00:10:10.381
but control them, and go out
and live the life you deserve.

00:10:11.944 --> 00:10:16.111
Choose to win, control your
thinking, and go win big.

00:10:17.861 --> 00:10:19.892
- And whenever people
reach out to me and say

00:10:19.892 --> 00:10:22.738
I'm doubting what I'm doing, I say well,

00:10:22.738 --> 00:10:25.584
congratulations, you're a human being.

00:10:25.584 --> 00:10:26.843
That's what it means to be a human.

00:10:26.843 --> 00:10:27.676
- High five.

00:10:27.676 --> 00:10:29.685
- You doubt what you do, it's
that voice inside our head.

00:10:29.685 --> 00:10:32.254
It's innate in all of us, we're born

00:10:32.254 --> 00:10:34.972
with the imposter syndrome, so we don't

00:10:34.972 --> 00:10:37.737
walk outside in the dark
with a saber-tooth tiger.

00:10:37.737 --> 00:10:39.892
It's like there's a voice
saying don't walk outside,

00:10:39.892 --> 00:10:41.676
it's dangerous, but we
don't live in that same

00:10:41.676 --> 00:10:44.153
world anymore, but we still
have that inside our head.

00:10:44.153 --> 00:10:46.751
And that's fine, but we
need to learn not to let

00:10:46.751 --> 00:10:49.471
it control our lives,
but to embrace that fear.

00:10:49.471 --> 00:10:51.091
So I still have it every single day.

00:10:51.091 --> 00:10:54.177
We talked about my revenue last month,

00:10:54.177 --> 00:10:58.344
I still wake up and say man,
should I do this webinar?

00:11:00.561 --> 00:11:02.836
I have these doubts and these fears,

00:11:02.836 --> 00:11:04.084
and that's just a reality and I've

00:11:04.084 --> 00:11:05.677
just learned to embrace that.

00:11:05.677 --> 00:11:06.563
- What's the first step to overcoming

00:11:06.563 --> 00:11:08.646
the fear or transforming the fear?

00:11:08.646 --> 00:11:11.529
- To witness it, to be the nonjudgmental

00:11:11.529 --> 00:11:14.206
witness of it, to look at it and say

00:11:14.206 --> 00:11:16.850
something's got to give, right?

00:11:16.850 --> 00:11:21.017
So if you're unwilling to
look at your fear head-on

00:11:22.254 --> 00:11:25.546
and honor it and, I always
say, if you don't show

00:11:25.546 --> 00:11:27.861
up for what's up it will keep showing up.

00:11:27.861 --> 00:11:30.422
So looking and saying I
witness my resistance,

00:11:30.422 --> 00:11:32.374
and you see that fear as resistance,

00:11:32.374 --> 00:11:36.207
fear is a resistance to
what it is you desire.

00:11:37.095 --> 00:11:39.003
And in the absence of
resistance you become

00:11:39.003 --> 00:11:40.911
a magnet for what you desire.

00:11:40.911 --> 00:11:43.148
When you let go of that
fear and you transcend

00:11:43.148 --> 00:11:45.626
that fear that's when you start to become

00:11:45.626 --> 00:11:48.027
a super attractor,
that's when you start to

00:11:48.027 --> 00:11:52.923
let what is truly of essence
for you into your life,

00:11:52.923 --> 00:11:54.345
what is truly of service
for you into your life,

00:11:54.345 --> 00:11:56.253
what is true happiness into your life.

00:11:56.253 --> 00:11:58.650
And so looking at the fear, witnessing it,

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:00.062
and calling it by it's name,

00:12:00.062 --> 00:12:02.295
and even if you don't have the tools yet,

00:12:02.295 --> 00:12:04.039
what happens is when you look at the fear

00:12:04.039 --> 00:12:07.110
and your like, oh I see this
fear, I see this resistance,

00:12:07.110 --> 00:12:08.847
I see how it's blocking my life,

00:12:08.847 --> 00:12:10.790
and I choose to see it differently.

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:12.575
That's when you're listening
to an audio like this.

00:12:12.575 --> 00:12:14.566
That's when a book like yours
will fall off the shelf.

00:12:14.566 --> 00:12:15.953
